    "title": "Charges dropped against former NFL player arrested for alleged altercation at school football practice - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jessica Patterson ,\n6 hours ago\nVideo of previous coverage.\nPUTNAM COUNTY, W.Va. (WOWK) – Charges have been dropped against a former Marshall standout and NFL player in Putnam County.\nAccording to Putnam County Prosecutor Kristina Raynes, she, Chris Massey and his attorney reached an agreement to drop the misdemeanor charges against Massey if he agreed not to pursue charges or a lawsuit against a deputy sheriff and former Winfield Middle School football coach.\nFormer NFL player arrested for alleged altercation with off-duty Putnam County deputy at school football practice The agreement also states that Massey has agreed not to pursue a lawsuit against the Putnam County Board of Education.\nA criminal complaint from Putnam County Magistrate Court filed last month said Massey, of Winfield, had been charged with obstructing an officer, battery, trespassing – asked to leave, and disorderly conduct.\nThe charges stemmed from an argument and altercation with the coach regarding Massey’s son’s football practice. The complaint stated Massey had been asked to leave multiple times before he was arrested.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFXRtv.",
